{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-31348","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-41554","text":"RFC — Evidence Residency ("},{"id":"spn-41555","marks":["code"],"text":"residency.repository.v1"},{"id":"spn-41556","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-31349","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41557","marks":["bold"],"text":"Status."},{"id":"spn-41558","text":" Ruled (user, 2026-07-23). This RFC freezes the first non-TRVM TRAAVIIS environment "},{"id":"spn-41559","marks":["italic"],"text":"before any code is written"},{"id":"spn-41560","text":". It scopes exactly one task, one one-shot agent interface, and the snapshot / output / verifier / reward / replayability contracts. Nothing here requires WallRiderLang lowering or TRVM interaction-calculus reduction. Code is held until these contracts are frozen."}]},{"id":"blk-31350","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41561","marks":["bold"],"text":"Thesis."},{"id":"spn-41562","text":" TRAAVIIS is an "},{"id":"spn-41563","marks":["bold"],"text":"evidence-grade environment for evaluating agents"},{"id":"spn-41564","text":". Its value is not \"deterministic worlds\" but: "},{"id":"spn-41565","marks":["italic"],"text":"an agent's work should leave inspectable evidence that survives replay, verification, disagreement, and human review."},{"id":"spn-41566","text":" Evidence Residency is the first environment that makes that concrete for a real repository, and it is deliberately "},{"id":"spn-41567","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-41568","text":" a TRVM world."}]},{"id":"blk-31351","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-41569","text":"1. Substrate ruling — TRAAVIIS is substrate-neutral"}]},{"id":"blk-31352","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41570","text":"TRAAVIIS evaluates over multiple substrates. TRVM is one — uniquely strong, but no longer the definition of everything TRAAVIIS can evaluate."}]},{"id":"blk-31353","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"TRAAVIIS\nsubstrate-neutral evaluation and evidence layer\n        │\n        ├── TRVM substrate            (trvm.world.v1)\n        │     sem · scen · film\n        │     reference · native · oracle\n        │\n        └── Residency substrate       (residency.repository.v1)\n              snapshot · finding · patch · trace\n              citations · patch · tests · identity"},{"id":"blk-31354","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41571","marks":["code"],"text":"residency.repository.v1"},{"id":"spn-41572","text":" is an "},{"id":"spn-41573","marks":["bold"],"text":"external evidence environment orchestrated by TRAAVIIS"},{"id":"spn-41574","text":". TRAAVIIS prepares a frozen subject, runs an agent command in a controlled workspace, collects evidence, and checks it with external deterministic verifiers. It does not fold anything through "},{"id":"spn-41575","marks":["code"],"text":"ic_ref"},{"id":"spn-41576","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-41577","marks":["code"],"text":"ic32"},{"id":"spn-41578","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-31355","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-41579","text":"2. The common ladder (shared) vs substrate-specific artifacts"}]},{"id":"blk-31356","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41580","text":"Four constructs are "},{"id":"spn-41581","marks":["bold"],"text":"shared"},{"id":"spn-41582","text":" across every substrate:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-31358","spans":[{"id":"spn-41583","text":"construct"}]},{"id":"blk-31359","spans":[{"id":"spn-41584","text":"question it answers"}]}],"id":"blk-31357","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-31360","spans":[{"id":"spn-41585","marks":["code"],"text":"TaskSpecV1"}]},{"id":"blk-31361","spans":[{"id":"spn-41586","text":"what must be done?"}]}],[{"id":"blk-31362","spans":[{"id":"spn-41587","marks":["code"],"text":"RewardSpecV1"}]},{"id":"blk-31363","spans":[{"id":"spn-41588","text":"how is admissible evidence scored?"}]}],[{"id":"blk-31364","spans":[{"id":"spn-41589","marks":["code"],"text":"SubstrateProfileV1"}]},{"id":"blk-31365","spans":[{"id":"spn-41590","text":"how is the subject prepared and evidence collected?"}]}],[{"id":"blk-31366","spans":[{"id":"spn-41591","marks":["code"],"text":"EpisodeReceiptV1"}]},{"id":"blk-31367","spans":[{"id":"spn-41592","text":"what happened, what was produced, what passed, what score?"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-31368","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41593","text":"Substrate-specific evidence lives "},{"id":"spn-41594","marks":["bold"],"text":"below"},{"id":"spn-41595","text":" the shared ladder:"}]},{"id":"blk-31369","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"TRVM       sem · scen · film\nResidency  snap · trace · finding · patch"},{"id":"blk-31370","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-41596","text":"2a. Correction — "},{"id":"spn-41597","marks":["code"],"text":"film-…"},{"id":"spn-41598","text":" is TRVM-only; the neutral trace is "},{"id":"spn-41599","marks":["code"],"text":"trace-…"}]},{"id":"blk-31371","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41600","text":"A "},{"id":"spn-41601","marks":["bold"],"text":"`film-…` is a TRVM deterministic-execution artifact"},{"id":"spn-41602","text":" and stays that way. It does "},{"id":"spn-41603","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-41604","text":" generalize to arbitrary substrates. The substrate-neutral observable record is a "},{"id":"spn-41605","marks":["bold"],"text":"`trace-…`"},{"id":"spn-41606","text":". The "},{"id":"spn-41607","marks":["bold"],"text":"shared"},{"id":"spn-41608","text":" object is the "},{"id":"spn-41609","marks":["bold"],"text":"`episode-…`"},{"id":"spn-41610","text":" receipt, which references whichever substrate-specific evidence exists plus a "},{"id":"spn-41611","marks":["code"],"text":"substrate_profile"},{"id":"spn-41612","text":". We do not pretend the underlying execution mechanisms are identical."}]},{"id":"blk-31372","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-41613","text":"3. Three meanings of \"replay\" (freeze this distinction)"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-31374","spans":[{"id":"spn-41614","text":"level"}]},{"id":"blk-31375","spans":[{"id":"spn-41615","text":"meaning"}]},{"id":"blk-31376","spans":[{"id":"spn-41616","text":"who supports it"}]}],"id":"blk-31373","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-31377","spans":[{"id":"spn-41617","marks":["bold"],"text":"exact replay"}]},{"id":"blk-31378","spans":[{"id":"spn-41618","text":"re-running canonical inputs reproduces the same state trajectory and film"}]},{"id":"blk-31379","spans":[{"id":"spn-41619","text":"TRVM"}]}],[{"id":"blk-31380","spans":[{"id":"spn-41620","marks":["bold"],"text":"action replay"}]},{"id":"blk-31381","spans":[{"id":"spn-41621","text":"recorded tool calls are reapplied against the same frozen snapshot"}]},{"id":"blk-31382","spans":[{"id":"spn-41622","text":"a controlled Residency runner, "},{"id":"spn-41623","marks":["italic"],"text":"later"}]}],[{"id":"blk-31383","spans":[{"id":"spn-41624","marks":["bold"],"text":"verification replay"}]},{"id":"blk-31384","spans":[{"id":"spn-41625","text":"the submitted finding, patch and receipts are re-checked against the frozen snapshot"}]},{"id":"blk-31385","spans":[{"id":"spn-41626","marks":["bold"],"text":"Residency v1"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-31386","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41627","marks":["bold"],"text":"Residency v1 promises only verification replay."},{"id":"spn-41628","text":" We do "},{"id":"spn-41629","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-41630","text":" promise deterministic replay of an arbitrary external coding-agent process — shell tools, package registries, clocks, and OS behaviour make that a much larger claim. Residency v1 honestly promises:"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-31388","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41631","text":"The evidence and outcome can be independently reverified."}]}],"id":"blk-31387","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-31389","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41632","marks":["code"],"text":"EpisodeReceiptV1.replayability"},{"id":"spn-41633","text":" records which level applies ("},{"id":"spn-41634","marks":["code"],"text":"exact"},{"id":"spn-41635","text":" for TRVM, "},{"id":"spn-41636","marks":["code"],"text":"verification"},{"id":"spn-41637","text":" for Residency v1)."}]},{"id":"blk-31390","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-41638","text":"4. Frozen subject — "},{"id":"spn-41639","marks":["code"],"text":"SnapshotV1"},{"id":"spn-41640","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-41641","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-…"}]},{"id":"blk-31391","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41642","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-…"},{"id":"spn-41643","text":" seals "},{"id":"spn-41644","marks":["bold"],"text":"only the subject"},{"id":"spn-41645","text":" — the repository the agent sees — "},{"id":"spn-41646","marks":["bold"],"text":"not the evaluation procedure"},{"id":"spn-41647","text":". The same frozen repository must remain the same "},{"id":"spn-41648","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-…"},{"id":"spn-41649","text":" even when evaluated under a different test plan."}]},{"id":"blk-31392","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{ \"snapshot_version\": \"residency.snapshot.v1\",\n  \"snapshot_id\": \"snap-…\",\n  \"files\": { \"<relpath>\": \"<content-hash>\", … },\n  \"exclusions\": [ \"<glob>\", … ],\n  \"file_modes\": { \"<relpath>\": \"0755\", … },\n  \"base_revision\": \"<vcs-rev or null>\",\n  \"visible_config\": { … } }"},{"id":"blk-31393","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41650","text":"Seal: repository bytes, normalized relative paths, file modes, exclusions, base revision if available, task-visible repository config. "},{"id":"spn-41651","marks":["bold"],"text":"Do not seal"},{"id":"spn-41652","text":" timestamps or absolute machine paths — they would make the snapshot machine-specific without changing its meaning. "},{"id":"spn-41653","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-…"},{"id":"spn-41654","text":" is a content hash of the canonical sealed bytes."}]},{"id":"blk-31394","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41655","marks":["bold"],"text":"Ownership split (erratum)."},{"id":"spn-41656","text":" The evaluation procedure lives in "},{"id":"spn-41657","marks":["code"],"text":"TaskSpecV1"},{"id":"spn-41658","text":", not the snapshot:"}]},{"id":"blk-31395","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-31397","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41659","marks":["bold"],"text":"`SnapshotV1`"},{"id":"spn-41660","text":" seals — repository bytes, relative paths, file modes,"}]}],"id":"blk-31396","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-31398","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41661","text":"exclusions, base revision, task-visible repository config."}]},{"id":"blk-31399","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-31401","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41662","marks":["bold"],"text":"`TaskSpecV1`"},{"id":"spn-41663","text":" seals — declared test commands, required toolchain"}]}],"id":"blk-31400","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-31402","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41664","text":"constraints, the verifier plan, and the agent execution policy (§7)."}]},{"id":"blk-31403","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-31405","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41665","marks":["bold"],"text":"`EpisodeReceiptV1`"},{"id":"spn-41666","text":" records — "},{"id":"spn-41667","marks":["italic"],"text":"actual"},{"id":"spn-41668","text":" toolchain versions, "},{"id":"spn-41669","marks":["italic"],"text":"actual"},{"id":"spn-41670","text":" verifier"}]}],"id":"blk-31404","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-31406","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41671","text":"versions, command exit codes, and platform facts relevant to verification."}]},{"id":"blk-31407","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41672","text":"This yields the right mutation behaviour:"}]},{"id":"blk-31408","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"change repository bytes   → snap / task / episode may move\nchange test command       → task / episode move ; snap unchanged\nrun on a different actual toolchain → episode moves ; task and snap stable"},{"id":"blk-31409","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-41673","text":"5. Agent outputs — "},{"id":"spn-41674","marks":["code"],"text":"FindingV1"},{"id":"spn-41675","text":", "},{"id":"spn-41676","marks":["code"],"text":"PatchV1"},{"id":"spn-41677","text":", "},{"id":"spn-41678","marks":["code"],"text":"TraceV1"}]},{"id":"blk-31410","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"FindingV1 → finding-…    structured claims + citations (not only prose)\nPatchV1   → patch-…      a unified diff that applies to a clean snapshot copy\nTraceV1   → trace-…      substrate-neutral record of observable process events"},{"id":"blk-31411","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41679","marks":["code"],"text":"FindingV1"},{"id":"spn-41680","text":" must carry "},{"id":"spn-41681","marks":["bold"],"text":"structured"},{"id":"spn-41682","text":" claims and citations, each citation resolving to exact supporting material inside the snapshot. Spans are "},{"id":"spn-41683","marks":["bold"],"text":"1-based inclusive line ranges"},{"id":"spn-41684","text":" expressed as an explicit object (never an ambiguous two-element array), and the "},{"id":"spn-41685","marks":["code"],"text":"quote"},{"id":"spn-41686","text":" must match the normalized snapshot bytes exactly:"}]},{"id":"blk-31412","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{ \"finding_version\": \"residency.finding.v1\",\n  \"finding_id\": \"finding-…\",\n  \"claims\": [ { \"statement\": \"…\",\n                \"citations\": [ { \"path\": \"spec/WRL_CORE_0.1.md\",\n                                 \"start_line\": 120, \"end_line\": 138,\n                                 \"quote\": \"…\" } ] } ] }"},{"id":"blk-31413","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41687","marks":["code"],"text":"TraceV1"},{"id":"spn-41688","text":" records observable events — enough to review and to drive "},{"id":"spn-41689","marks":["italic"],"text":"action replay"},{"id":"spn-41690","text":" later, without claiming determinism now."}]},{"id":"blk-31414","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-41691","text":"5a. Canonical evidence rules (freeze before generating any IDs)"}]},{"id":"blk-31415","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41692","marks":["bold"],"text":"Snapshot paths."},{"id":"spn-41693","text":" UTF-8 relative POSIX paths; no absolute paths; no "},{"id":"spn-41694","marks":["code"],"text":".."},{"id":"spn-41695","text":"; "},{"id":"spn-41696","marks":["code"],"text":"/"},{"id":"spn-41697","text":" separator on every platform; explicit symlink policy (v1: symlinks excluded); explicit line-ending policy (v1: normalize to LF for text, byte-exact for declared-binary)."}]},{"id":"blk-31416","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41698","marks":["bold"],"text":"Citations."},{"id":"spn-41699","text":" 1-based inclusive line ranges as "},{"id":"spn-41700","marks":["code"],"text":"{start_line, end_line}"},{"id":"spn-41701","text":"; the quoted text matches the normalized snapshot bytes exactly."}]},{"id":"blk-31417","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41702","marks":["bold"],"text":"Patches."},{"id":"spn-41703","text":" Unified diff; relative paths only; no timestamps; fixed "},{"id":"spn-41704","marks":["code"],"text":"a/"},{"id":"spn-41705","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-41706","marks":["code"],"text":"b/"},{"id":"spn-41707","text":" prefixes; LF line endings; "},{"id":"spn-41708","marks":["bold"],"text":"no binary patches in v1"},{"id":"spn-41709","text":"; canonical file ordering (sorted by POSIX path)."}]},{"id":"blk-31418","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41710","marks":["bold"],"text":"Traces."},{"id":"spn-41711","text":" Exclude volatile timestamps and host paths from "},{"id":"spn-41712","marks":["code"],"text":"trace-…"},{"id":"spn-41713","text":" identity. The canonical trace records deterministic events only:"}]},{"id":"blk-31419","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"command argv · relative cwd · declared environment keys · exit code\nstdout digest · stderr digest · files-created digest · files-modified digest\nresult-file digest"},{"id":"blk-31420","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41714","text":"Human-readable timed logs may exist beside the canonical trace "},{"id":"spn-41715","marks":["bold"],"text":"without"},{"id":"spn-41716","text":" entering its identity."}]},{"id":"blk-31421","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-41717","text":"6. Verifier applicability — four states"}]},{"id":"blk-31422","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41718","text":"Every verifier returns exactly one of:"}]},{"id":"blk-31423","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"pass · fail · not_applicable · error"},{"id":"blk-31424","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41719","marks":["code"],"text":"error"},{"id":"spn-41720","text":" "},{"id":"spn-41721","marks":["bold"],"text":"must remain distinct"},{"id":"spn-41722","text":" from "},{"id":"spn-41723","marks":["code"],"text":"fail"},{"id":"spn-41724","text":": an unavailable test runner is not evidence that the candidate patch is wrong. "},{"id":"spn-41725","marks":["code"],"text":"not_applicable"},{"id":"spn-41726","text":" is coverage honesty (e.g. "},{"id":"spn-41727","marks":["code"],"text":"native"},{"id":"spn-41728","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-41729","marks":["code"],"text":"oracle"},{"id":"spn-41730","text":" on a Residency episode). The receipt's verification map is "},{"id":"spn-41731","marks":["bold"],"text":"total"},{"id":"spn-41732","text":" — every declared verifier reports one of the four."}]},{"id":"blk-31425","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41733","text":"Residency v1 verifier set:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-31427","spans":[{"id":"spn-41734","text":"verifier"}]},{"id":"blk-31428","spans":[{"id":"spn-41735","text":"checks"}]}],"id":"blk-31426","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-31429","spans":[{"id":"spn-41736","marks":["code"],"text":"citations"}]},{"id":"blk-31430","spans":[{"id":"spn-41737","text":"every finding citation resolves and the quote matches source"}]}],[{"id":"blk-31431","spans":[{"id":"spn-41738","marks":["code"],"text":"patch"}]},{"id":"blk-31432","spans":[{"id":"spn-41739","text":"the patch applies cleanly to a fresh copy of "},{"id":"spn-41740","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-…"}]}],[{"id":"blk-31433","spans":[{"id":"spn-41741","marks":["code"],"text":"tests"}]},{"id":"blk-31434","spans":[{"id":"spn-41742","text":"the declared "},{"id":"spn-41743","marks":["code"],"text":"test_commands"},{"id":"spn-41744","text":" pass on the patched copy"}]}],[{"id":"blk-31435","spans":[{"id":"spn-41745","marks":["code"],"text":"identity"}]},{"id":"blk-31436","spans":[{"id":"spn-41746","text":"semantic identity moved only within allowed domains"}]}],[{"id":"blk-31437","spans":[{"id":"spn-41747","marks":["code"],"text":"native"}]},{"id":"blk-31438","spans":[{"id":"spn-41748","marks":["code"],"text":"not_applicable"},{"id":"spn-41749","text":" (TRVM-only)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-31439","spans":[{"id":"spn-41750","marks":["code"],"text":"oracle"}]},{"id":"blk-31440","spans":[{"id":"spn-41751","marks":["code"],"text":"not_applicable"},{"id":"spn-41752","text":" (TRVM-only)"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-31441","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41753","text":"The "},{"id":"spn-41754","marks":["code"],"text":"identity"},{"id":"spn-41755","text":" verifier is where TRVM's guarantees re-enter: if the task touches a WRL world, the frozen "},{"id":"spn-41756","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-…"},{"id":"spn-41757","text":" domains that must not move are checked with the existing Forge re-lower — a Residency episode can "},{"id":"spn-41758","marks":["italic"],"text":"depend on"},{"id":"spn-41759","text":" a TRVM identity check without "},{"id":"spn-41760","marks":["italic"],"text":"being"},{"id":"spn-41761","text":" a TRVM fold."}]},{"id":"blk-31442","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-41762","text":"6a. Verifier state → reward behavior (frozen)"}]},{"id":"blk-31443","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41763","text":"The four verifier states map to reward behavior by a fixed table. "},{"id":"spn-41764","marks":["bold"],"text":"A test runner failure is not evidence that the agent's work was incorrect"},{"id":"spn-41765","text":" — it is substrate unavailability, and it must never be scored as a "},{"id":"spn-41766","marks":["code"],"text":"fail"},{"id":"spn-41767","text":"."}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-31445","spans":[{"id":"spn-41768","text":"State"}]},{"id":"blk-31446","spans":[{"id":"spn-41769","text":"Reward behavior"}]}],"id":"blk-31444","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-31447","spans":[{"id":"spn-41770","marks":["code"],"text":"pass"}]},{"id":"blk-31448","spans":[{"id":"spn-41771","text":"signal receives its positive value"}]}],[{"id":"blk-31449","spans":[{"id":"spn-41772","marks":["code"],"text":"fail"}]},{"id":"blk-31450","spans":[{"id":"spn-41773","text":"signal receives zero; applicable floors/caps run"}]}],[{"id":"blk-31451","spans":[{"id":"spn-41774","marks":["code"],"text":"not_applicable"}]},{"id":"blk-31452","spans":[{"id":"spn-41775","text":"allowed only when the task declares the signal non-required"}]}],[{"id":"blk-31453","spans":[{"id":"spn-41776","marks":["code"],"text":"error"}]},{"id":"blk-31454","spans":[{"id":"spn-41777","text":"episode "},{"id":"spn-41778","marks":["code"],"text":"status"},{"id":"spn-41779","text":" becomes "},{"id":"spn-41780","marks":["code"],"text":"error"},{"id":"spn-41781","text":"; reward is "},{"id":"spn-41782","marks":["code"],"text":"null"},{"id":"spn-41783","text":", not "},{"id":"spn-41784","marks":["code"],"text":"0"}]}],[{"id":"blk-31455","spans":[{"id":"spn-41785","text":"required verifier returns "},{"id":"spn-41786","marks":["code"],"text":"not_applicable"}]},{"id":"blk-31456","spans":[{"id":"spn-41787","text":"invalid task configuration ("},{"id":"spn-41788","marks":["code"],"text":"status: invalid"},{"id":"spn-41789","text":")"}]}],[{"id":"blk-31457","spans":[{"id":"spn-41790","text":"snapshot tampering"}]},{"id":"blk-31458","spans":[{"id":"spn-41791","text":"invalid episode ("},{"id":"spn-41792","marks":["code"],"text":"status: invalid"},{"id":"spn-41793","text":"); reward "},{"id":"spn-41794","marks":["code"],"text":"0"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-31459","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41795","text":"The distinction between "},{"id":"spn-41796","marks":["code"],"text":"null"},{"id":"spn-41797","text":" (an "},{"id":"spn-41798","marks":["code"],"text":"error"},{"id":"spn-41799","text":" episode: scoring could not be computed) and "},{"id":"spn-41800","marks":["code"],"text":"0"},{"id":"spn-41801","text":" (a real "},{"id":"spn-41802","marks":["code"],"text":"fail"},{"id":"spn-41803","text":" or a tamper) is load-bearing. Downstream aggregation must drop "},{"id":"spn-41804","marks":["code"],"text":"null"},{"id":"spn-41805","text":"-reward episodes, never average them in as zeros."}]},{"id":"blk-31460","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-41806","text":"7. Reward — deterministic, decomposable, no LLM prose judging"}]},{"id":"blk-31461","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41807","marks":["code"],"text":"RewardSpecV1"},{"id":"spn-41808","text":" for the first task is a "},{"id":"spn-41809","marks":["bold"],"text":"canonical keyed signal map"},{"id":"spn-41810","text":" (see "},{"id":"spn-41811","marks":["code"],"text":"RFC_TRAAVIIS_ARTIFACTS.md"},{"id":"spn-41812","text":" §2): each key binds one verifier result to one weight. The identifiers are load-bearing — renaming a signal moves "},{"id":"spn-41813","marks":["code"],"text":"rew-…"},{"id":"spn-41814","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-31462","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"citations             → residency.citations.v1   0.25\npatch                 → residency.patch.v1        0.20\ntests                 → residency.tests.v1        0.30\nidentity              → residency.identity.v1     0.15\nfinding_completeness  → residency.finding.v1      0.10"},{"id":"blk-31463","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41815","marks":["bold"],"text":"`finding completeness` means required structured fields + evidence coverage"},{"id":"spn-41816","text":", never prose quality judged by another model. No signal in Residency v1 calls an LLM; every signal is a pure function over sealed evidence."}]},{"id":"blk-31464","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41817","marks":["bold"],"text":"Hard floors (caps, applied after the weighted sum):"}]},{"id":"blk-31465","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"patch does not apply        → reward ≤ 0.25\ncitations do not resolve    → reward ≤ 0.25\nrequired tests regress      → reward ≤ 0.40\ntampered snapshot           → reward = 0 and episode marked invalid"},{"id":"blk-31466","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41818","marks":["code"],"text":"rew-…"},{"id":"spn-41819","text":" is the content hash of the canonical "},{"id":"spn-41820","marks":["code"],"text":"RewardSpecV1"},{"id":"spn-41821","text":" (weights + floors + verifier binding)."}]},{"id":"blk-31467","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-41822","text":"8. First task (one, narrow, bounded)"}]},{"id":"blk-31468","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"task: residency/wrl-spec-impl-inconsistency-001\n\nIdentify one real inconsistency between a frozen WallRiderLang specification and\nits implementation. Cite the exact conflicting evidence, propose the smallest\npatch, run the declared acceptance checks, and preserve identities that should\nnot move."},{"id":"blk-31469","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41823","text":"Bounded corpus, explicit success contract. The agent is "},{"id":"spn-41824","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-41825","text":" asked to search for any possible improvement — it is given a fixed snapshot and a single, checkable objective."}]},{"id":"blk-31470","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-41826","text":"9. Mutation laws (freeze; test-first before code)"}]},{"id":"blk-31471","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"change repository input\n  → snap / task / trace / finding / patch / episode may move\n\nchange task instructions\n  → task / episode move\n  → snap unchanged\n\nchange reward weights\n  → rew / episode move\n  → snap / trace / finding / patch unchanged\n\nchange agent output\n  → finding / patch / trace / episode move\n  → task / snap unchanged\n\nrerun the SAME verifier versions over identical frozen artifacts\n  UNDER identical canonical execution facts\n  → episode identity remains stable\n\nchange verifier implementation version\n  OR change canonical execution facts (toolchain, exit codes, platform)\n  → episode moves\n  → underlying evidence artifacts (snap / trace / finding / patch) unchanged"},{"id":"blk-31472","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41827","text":"The stability law is stated precisely because the receipt records "},{"id":"spn-41828","marks":["code"],"text":"execution_facts"},{"id":"spn-41829","text":". Stability holds only when "},{"id":"spn-41830","marks":["bold"],"text":"both"},{"id":"spn-41831","text":" the verifier versions "},{"id":"spn-41832","marks":["bold"],"text":"and"},{"id":"spn-41833","text":" the "},{"id":"spn-41834","marks":["italic"],"text":"canonical"},{"id":"spn-41835","text":" execution facts are identical; changing either moves the "},{"id":"spn-41836","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-…"},{"id":"spn-41837","text":". (The "},{"id":"spn-41838","marks":["italic"],"text":"volatile"},{"id":"spn-41839","text":" execution facts — wall-clock, absolute paths, transient PIDs — are excluded from the hash, so they never move it.) This reconciles with the already-stated law that a different "},{"id":"spn-41840","marks":["bold"],"text":"actual"},{"id":"spn-41841","text":" toolchain moves the episode: "},{"id":"spn-41842","marks":["bold"],"text":"verifier versions and canonical execution facts are recorded in the receipt"},{"id":"spn-41843","text":", so a scoring-logic change or a toolchain change is auditable and moves the "},{"id":"spn-41844","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-…"},{"id":"spn-41845","text":" without rewriting what the agent actually produced."}]},{"id":"blk-31473","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-41846","text":"10. "},{"id":"spn-41847","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs eval-one"},{"id":"spn-41848","text":" — the one-shot interface (first implementation)"}]},{"id":"blk-31474","kind":"code","language":"bash","text":"trvs eval-one residency/wrl-spec-impl-inconsistency-001.json \\\n  --agent-command \"./stub-agent\""},{"id":"blk-31475","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41849","text":"The agent command receives a frozen workspace and emits one structured final result:"}]},{"id":"blk-31476","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{ \"format\": \"traaviis.agent-result.v1\",\n  \"finding\": { \"summary\": \"…\", \"citations\": [ … ] },\n  \"patch_path\": \"candidate.patch\" }"},{"id":"blk-31477","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41850","text":"TRAAVIIS then, independently and deterministically:"}]},{"id":"blk-31478","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-31480","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41851","text":"snapshots the starting repository → "},{"id":"spn-41852","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-…"},{"id":"spn-41853","text":";"}]}],"id":"blk-31479","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-31482","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41854","text":"runs the command in a controlled workspace;"}]}],"id":"blk-31481","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-31484","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41855","text":"captures observable process events → "},{"id":"spn-41856","marks":["code"],"text":"trace-…"},{"id":"spn-41857","text":";"}]}],"id":"blk-31483","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-31486","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41858","text":"reads the proposed finding and patch → "},{"id":"spn-41859","marks":["code"],"text":"finding-…"},{"id":"spn-41860","text":", "},{"id":"spn-41861","marks":["code"],"text":"patch-…"},{"id":"spn-41862","text":";"}]}],"id":"blk-31485","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-31488","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41863","text":"resolves citations against "},{"id":"spn-41864","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-…"},{"id":"spn-41865","text":";"}]}],"id":"blk-31487","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-31490","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41866","text":"applies the patch to a clean copy of "},{"id":"spn-41867","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-…"},{"id":"spn-41868","text":";"}]}],"id":"blk-31489","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-31492","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41869","text":"runs the declared "},{"id":"spn-41870","marks":["code"],"text":"test_commands"},{"id":"spn-41871","text":";"}]}],"id":"blk-31491","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-31494","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41872","text":"measures identity movement;"}]}],"id":"blk-31493","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-31496","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41873","text":"calculates the reward (weights + floors);"}]}],"id":"blk-31495","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-31498","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41874","text":"emits "},{"id":"spn-41875","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-…"},{"id":"spn-41876","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-31497","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-31499","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41877","text":"A richer interactive N-step action protocol (and the ORS adapter over the Episode Kernel) can follow "},{"id":"spn-41878","marks":["bold"],"text":"after"},{"id":"spn-41879","text":" this one-shot path works and is boring."}]},{"id":"blk-31500","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-41880","text":"10a. "},{"id":"spn-41881","marks":["code"],"text":"AgentRunPolicyV1"},{"id":"spn-41882","text":" — the frozen one-shot execution policy"}]},{"id":"blk-31501","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41883","text":"The task carries an "},{"id":"spn-41884","marks":["code"],"text":"agent_run_policy"},{"id":"spn-41885","text":" sub-document. It is part of the "},{"id":"spn-41886","marks":["code"],"text":"TaskSpecV1"},{"id":"spn-41887","text":" identity: changing how the agent is allowed to run changes "},{"id":"spn-41888","marks":["code"],"text":"task-…"},{"id":"spn-41889","text":". The runner enforces it; the receipt records what actually happened."}]},{"id":"blk-31502","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{ \"policy_version\": \"traaviis.agent-run-policy.v1\",\n  \"command_mode\": \"argv\",\n  \"shell\": false,\n  \"network\": \"disabled\",\n  \"timeout_seconds\": 900,\n  \"max_output_bytes\": 4194304,\n  \"environment\": { \"LANG\": \"C.UTF-8\", \"HOME\": \"/sandbox/home\" },\n  \"toolchain_profile\": \"residency.python-3.11.v1\",\n  \"writable_paths\": [\".\"],\n  \"result_path\": \"result.json\",\n  \"patch_path\": \"candidate.patch\" }"},{"id":"blk-31503","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41890","text":"Rules:"}]},{"id":"blk-31504","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-31506","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41891","marks":["bold"],"text":"`command_mode: argv`, `shell: false`"},{"id":"spn-41892","text":" — the agent command is an argv vector"}]}],"id":"blk-31505","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-31507","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41893","text":"executed without a shell. No shell interpolation is part of the contract."}]},{"id":"blk-31508","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-31510","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41894","marks":["bold"],"text":"`network: disabled`"},{"id":"spn-41895","text":" by default — a task that needs the network must declare"}]}],"id":"blk-31509","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-31511","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41896","text":"it explicitly, and that declaration moves "},{"id":"spn-41897","marks":["code"],"text":"task-…"},{"id":"spn-41898","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-31512","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-31514","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41899","marks":["bold"],"text":"`timeout_seconds` / `max_output_bytes`"},{"id":"spn-41900","text":" are hard bounds. Exceeding either"}]}],"id":"blk-31513","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-31515","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41901","text":"terminates the run; the episode records the termination reason and the affected verifier reports "},{"id":"spn-41902","marks":["code"],"text":"error"},{"id":"spn-41903","text":" (substrate unavailability), not "},{"id":"spn-41904","marks":["code"],"text":"fail"},{"id":"spn-41905","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-31516","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-31518","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41906","marks":["bold"],"text":"`environment` is a sealed key→value map, not a host allowlist."},{"id":"spn-41907","text":" Host"}]}],"id":"blk-31517","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-31519","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41908","text":"environment values ("},{"id":"spn-41909","marks":["code"],"text":"PATH"},{"id":"spn-41910","text":", "},{"id":"spn-41911","marks":["code"],"text":"HOME"},{"id":"spn-41912","text":", "},{"id":"spn-41913","marks":["code"],"text":"LANG"},{"id":"spn-41914","text":", …) are "},{"id":"spn-41915","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-41916","text":" inherited — their values could change behavior without entering "},{"id":"spn-41917","marks":["code"],"text":"task-…"},{"id":"spn-41918","text":", which would break the frozen-subject claim. Only the sealed keys with their "},{"id":"spn-41919","marks":["bold"],"text":"fixed, normalized values"},{"id":"spn-41920","text":" are exported; everything else is stripped. The runner constructs a controlled "},{"id":"spn-41921","marks":["code"],"text":"PATH"},{"id":"spn-41922","text":" from the "},{"id":"spn-41923","marks":["code"],"text":"toolchain_profile"},{"id":"spn-41924","text":"; it never inherits the host's arbitrary "},{"id":"spn-41925","marks":["code"],"text":"PATH"},{"id":"spn-41926","text":". An allowlist is safe only when "},{"id":"spn-41927","marks":["bold"],"text":"both"},{"id":"spn-41928","text":" the key "},{"id":"spn-41929","marks":["italic"],"text":"and"},{"id":"spn-41930","text":" its normalized value are fixed, which is exactly what a sealed map is."}]},{"id":"blk-31520","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-31522","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41931","marks":["bold"],"text":"`toolchain_profile`"},{"id":"spn-41932","text":" names the sealed toolchain (interpreter, package set)."}]}],"id":"blk-31521","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-31523","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41933","text":"The "},{"id":"spn-41934","marks":["bold"],"text":"actual resolved executables and versions"},{"id":"spn-41935","text":" go into the receipt's "},{"id":"spn-41936","marks":["code"],"text":"execution_facts"},{"id":"spn-41937","text":", so a toolchain drift is auditable and moves "},{"id":"spn-41938","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-…"},{"id":"spn-41939","text":" (see §9), while the "},{"id":"spn-41940","marks":["italic"],"text":"declared"},{"id":"spn-41941","text":" profile is part of "},{"id":"spn-41942","marks":["code"],"text":"task-…"},{"id":"spn-41943","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-31524","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-31526","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41944","marks":["bold"],"text":"`writable_paths`"},{"id":"spn-41945","text":" scopes filesystem mutation; writes outside the set are a"}]}],"id":"blk-31525","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-31527","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41946","text":"policy violation that invalidates the episode."}]},{"id":"blk-31528","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-31530","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41947","marks":["bold"],"text":"`result_path` / `patch_path`"},{"id":"spn-41948","text":" are where the runner reads the structured"}]}],"id":"blk-31529","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-31531","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41949","text":"result and the candidate patch after the process exits. Absence of a required output is a "},{"id":"spn-41950","marks":["code"],"text":"fail"},{"id":"spn-41951","text":" for the corresponding verifier, never an "},{"id":"spn-41952","marks":["code"],"text":"error"},{"id":"spn-41953","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-31532","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41954","text":"The distinction is deliberate: a "},{"id":"spn-41955","marks":["bold"],"text":"policy or substrate failure"},{"id":"spn-41956","text":" (timeout, output cap, missing runner) yields "},{"id":"spn-41957","marks":["code"],"text":"error"},{"id":"spn-41958","text":"; a "},{"id":"spn-41959","marks":["bold"],"text":"missing or malformed agent output"},{"id":"spn-41960","text":" yields "},{"id":"spn-41961","marks":["code"],"text":"fail"},{"id":"spn-41962","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-31533","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-41963","text":"11. Example receipts"}]},{"id":"blk-31534","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41964","marks":["bold"],"text":"TRVM episode"},{"id":"spn-41965","text":" (Golden Spinner, unchanged):"}]},{"id":"blk-31535","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{ \"episode_version\": \"traaviis.episode.v1\",\n  \"substrate_profile\": \"trvm.world.v1\",\n  \"task_id\": \"task-…\",\n  \"subject\": { \"world\": \"sem-…\", \"scenario\": \"scen-…\" },\n  \"trace\": \"film-…\",\n  \"verification\": { \"reference\": \"pass\", \"native\": \"pass\", \"oracle\": \"pass\" },\n  \"verifier_versions\": { \"reference\": \"1\", \"native\": \"1\", \"oracle\": \"1\" },\n  \"reward\": 1,\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"validity\": \"valid\",\n  \"replayability\": \"exact\",\n  \"execution_facts\": { \"reducer\": \"ic32\", \"epochs\": 9 } }"},{"id":"blk-31536","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41966","marks":["bold"],"text":"Evidence Residency episode:"}]},{"id":"blk-31537","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{ \"episode_version\": \"traaviis.episode.v1\",\n  \"substrate_profile\": \"residency.repository.v1\",\n  \"task_id\": \"task-…\",\n  \"subject\": { \"snapshot\": \"snap-…\" },\n  \"trace\": \"trace-…\",\n  \"outputs\": { \"finding\": \"finding-…\", \"patch\": \"patch-…\" },\n  \"verification\": { \"citations\": \"pass\", \"patch\": \"pass\", \"tests\": \"pass\",\n                    \"identity\": \"pass\",\n                    \"native\": \"not_applicable\", \"oracle\": \"not_applicable\" },\n  \"verifier_versions\": { \"citations\": \"1\", \"patch\": \"1\", \"tests\": \"1\", \"identity\": \"1\" },\n  \"reward\": 1.0,\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"validity\": \"valid\",\n  \"replayability\": \"verification\",\n  \"execution_facts\": { \"exit_code\": 0, \"platform\": \"linux-x86_64\",\n                       \"timed_out\": false, \"output_truncated\": false } }"},{"id":"blk-31538","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41967","marks":["code"],"text":"status"},{"id":"spn-41968","text":" is "},{"id":"spn-41969","marks":["code"],"text":"ok | error | invalid"},{"id":"spn-41970","text":"; "},{"id":"spn-41971","marks":["code"],"text":"validity"},{"id":"spn-41972","text":" is "},{"id":"spn-41973","marks":["code"],"text":"valid | invalid"},{"id":"spn-41974","text":". An "},{"id":"spn-41975","marks":["code"],"text":"error"},{"id":"spn-41976","text":" episode carries "},{"id":"spn-41977","marks":["code"],"text":"reward: null"},{"id":"spn-41978","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-31539","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41979","text":"Canonical "},{"id":"spn-41980","marks":["code"],"text":"execution_facts"},{"id":"spn-41981","text":" — including resolved toolchain versions, normalized platform, exit codes, timeout state, and output-truncation state — enter the "},{"id":"spn-41982","marks":["code"],"text":"episode_id"},{"id":"spn-41983","text":" hash. Volatile execution metadata — wall-clock timestamps, absolute paths, transient process IDs, and host-specific log locations — is excluded."}]},{"id":"blk-31540","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41984","text":"Same ladder, honest about different execution mechanisms."}]},{"id":"blk-31541","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-41985","text":"12. Held until this RFC is accepted"}]},{"id":"blk-31542","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-41986","text":"Not built now: the interactive N-step environment protocol, ORS/MCP adapters, batch "},{"id":"spn-41987","marks":["code"],"text":"eval"},{"id":"spn-41988","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-41989","marks":["code"],"text":"compare"},{"id":"spn-41990","text":", action replay, a second Residency task, process rewards, and any new identity category beyond "},{"id":"spn-41991","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-…"},{"id":"spn-41992","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-41993","marks":["code"],"text":"trace-…"},{"id":"spn-41994","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-41995","marks":["code"],"text":"finding-…"},{"id":"spn-41996","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-41997","marks":["code"],"text":"patch-…"},{"id":"spn-41998","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-41999","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-…"},{"id":"spn-42000","text":". Spinner Bench v0.7-5 proceeds independently and is not a blocker for this RFC."}]},{"id":"blk-31543","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-42001","text":"MIT licensed · TRAAVIIS Holdings · part of the [&] Protocol ecosystem."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaiera3wp5ekmuhl4oxgc7bzfjrkcusa6sx4on2nrv2swwfrepkh7i7esq","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}